%N A400234 Number of spanning trees in the 3 X n Klein bottle grid graph.
%C A400234 The 3 X n Klein bottle grid graph has 3n vertices arranged in a 3 X n grid with periodic boundary conditions in the vertical direction (forming a cylinder in each column) and antiperiodic boundary conditions with twist in the horizontal direction: (r, n-1) ~ (2-r, 0).
%C A400234 For n=1, the twist identification creates multi-edges between vertices 0 and 2, and a loop at vertex 1 (ignored in the spanning tree count). The resulting multigraph has 3 vertices and 5 edges, yielding a(1) = 7 spanning trees.
%C A400234 The sequence decomposes as a(n) = c_0(n) + c_1(n) + c_2(n) + c_3(n), where c_j(n) counts spanning trees using exactly j of the 3 twist edges. The twist-free component c_0(n) counts spanning trees of the cylinder C_3 X P_n (no twist edge used).
%H A400234 Andrew Howroyd, <a href="/A400234/b400234.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..500</a>
%H A400234 Eric Weisstein's World of Mathematics, <a href="https://mathworld.wolfram.com/SpanningTree.html">Spanning Tree</a>.
%H A400234 <a href="/index/Rec#order_06">Index entries for linear recurrences with constant coefficients</a>, signature (48,-624,1154,-624,48,-1).
%F A400234 G.f.: 7*x*(1 + 2*x - 48*x^2 + 2*x^3 + x^4)/((1 - x)^2*(1 - 23*x + x^2)^2). - _Andrew Howroyd_, Oct 31 2026
%e A400234 For n=1, the 3 X 1 Klein bottle grid has 3 vertices and 5 edges (including multi-edges from the twist). It has a(1) = 7 spanning trees.
%e A400234 For n=2, the 3 X 2 Klein bottle grid has 6 vertices and 12 edges. It has a(2) = 350 spanning trees.
%e A400234 For n=3, the 3 X 3 Klein bottle grid has 9 vertices and 18 edges. It has a(3) = 12096 spanning trees.
%t A400234 LinearRecurrence[{48, -624, 1154, -624, 48, -1}, {7, 350, 12096, 370300, 10626035, 292723200}, 20] (* _Paolo Xausa_, Nov 10 2026 *)
%o A400234 (Python) # uses C() from A401537
%o A400234 print([C(n,1) for n in range(1,12)]) # _Jean Lauro Muller_, Oct 31 2026
